# devops — concepts reference

## What DevOps means

A cultural sensibility: a unified, metrics-based approach to making
software efficiently and fearlessly, using as much automation as
possible. Many companies lack the discipline for a true DevOps culture
and use "DevOps Engineer" as a title for infrastructure engineers who
know AWS or Google Cloud.

## API — Application Programming Interface

A set of subroutines, communication protocols, and tools for building
software. APIs can receive web-based requests and send responses.

## REST — REpresentational State Transfer

An architectural style defining constraints for creating web services.
RESTful services provide interoperability between systems on the
internet.

## CRUD and HTTP methods

| CRUD   | HTTP method |
| ------ | ----------- |
| Create | POST        |
| Read   | GET         |
| Update | PUT         |
| Delete | DELETE      |

```sh
# CRUD against a REST API from the shell
curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"name":"homelab"}' http://mediaserver:8080/api/hosts
curl http://mediaserver:8080/api/hosts
curl -X PUT -d '{"name":"homelab2"}' http://mediaserver:8080/api/hosts/1
curl -X DELETE http://mediaserver:8080/api/hosts/1
```

## JSON — JavaScript Object Notation

An open-standard file format using human-readable text to transmit
data objects of attribute-value pairs and arrays.

## API token

A software token: an authentication device authorizing use of computer
services. An API token uniquely identifies an application requesting
access to your service.

## Agile project management

Working in smaller, multidisciplinary teams to achieve objectives more
quickly.

## Behavior-driven development (BDD)

Obtaining a clear understanding of desired software behavior through
discussion with stakeholders and collaboration among developers, QA,
and non-technical or business participants.

## Burndown chart

A line chart representing remaining work over time.

## Daily standup / scrum

Whole-team meeting at the same time, 15 minutes or less. Each member
answers: what did I do yesterday, what will I do today, what blocks me?

## Feature creep

When software becomes complicated and difficult to use from
accumulating features.

## Kanban

A visual workflow method: work items move across columns
(e.g. To Do → Doing → Done) with limits on work in progress.
